[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report as one issue. It holds three problems, each
needing its own fix, and each now has its own ticket. #4471 closed on 5 October: engineering fixed
the parser and retired the booking-v3 form. That ends two of the three.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day move is still open. Neither the parser fix nor retiring booking-v3 touches it, and
#4471 is closed, so new reports of it have no ticket to land in except #3.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How to tell them apart

**parser** (fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`): the tenant writes the day first
and the shared parser read the month first, so 7 April came out as 4 July. Any channel, any
day-first tenant.

**hint** (won't fix: booking-v3 retired): the tenant ran booking-v3, whose date field showed the
hint `MM/DD/YYYY`. People typed the month first, as the hint asked, and the form read it the
tenant's way, day first. Form only, booking-v3 tenants only. Intake tagged them by the reporter's
browser, so the "tagged as" column on #4471 doesn't match: go by tenant and channel, as
`causes.ts` does.

**one-day** (open): the date moves back one day, not across months: Tuesday 12 May shows as
Monday 11 May; a meeting reaches Lisbon as Tuesday and Toronto as Monday. Nothing is flipped, so
neither fix touches it. The desk noted these reports (`desk-notes.json`) and counts them under the
parser by tenant, which is why they closed with #4471.

## Why they ended up together

Triage merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and all three problems arrive under the same subjects: "Date is wrong", "Wrong day on the
invite". That page hasn't been reviewed since June 2024. Until a new decision replaces it,
check tenant and channel before merging a date report into a ticket.

